  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening a survivor-centred, holistic response to conflict-related sexual violence in the Ukraine crisis</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.Improved access to quality holistic care for survivors of conflict related sexual violence  in the short and  longer-term  by supporting the creation of  a National Centre of Excellence in Kyiv and a holistic one-stop-centre in Lviv, as well as providing support to other key entry points and facilities in the holistic care referral pathway. 2.Strengthened knowledge and skills of professionals to deliver trauma-aware, survivor-centred, holistic care for survivors of conflict-related sexual violence by developing and implementing a comprehensive Training of Trainers package and making digital resources, tools and follow-up available.3.Awareness raised of the availability of holistic care at community level and improve access to services through support to state, civil society and survivor-led activities including mobile teams, hotlines and sensitisation activities.</narrative>
  </description>
